# What NOT to publish. Same syntax as .gitignore, read by wrangler at deploy.
#
# The assets directory is the repo root (see wrangler.jsonc), so without this
# file every source file in the project would be fetchable on picsel.co.uk:
# the planning documents, the build tooling, the client list. This is the list
# of things that live in the repo but are nobody's business on the web.
#
# The rule for editing it: if a browser is ever told to load a file, it must
# NOT appear here. Everything the pages reference is root-relative, so a wrong
# entry here shows up as a missing stylesheet on the live site and nowhere in
# local testing. Check against the src= and href= values in the built HTML.

# Dependencies. Installed on the build machine, never served.
node_modules

# The build step itself, and the data it reads. site.config.js and projects.js
# are imported by tools/build.js at build time only; their contents are already
# baked into the generated HTML, so publishing them serves the same facts twice
# and hands over the phone number and client list in machine-readable form.
tools
site.config.js
projects.js

# Planning and instruction documents. plan-picsel-site.md and CLAUDE.md read as
# internal notes because they are.
*.md

# npm metadata. Reveals the toolchain, serves no visitor.
package.json
package-lock.json

# Repo and editor plumbing.
.claude
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# This file and the deploy config. Not secret, just not content.
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc
